    "product": {
      "id": 1122274,
      "name": "Garlic Scapes",
      "description": "Garlic scapes are the edible, curly flower stalks of hardneck garlic, harvested in late spring/early summer for a milder, sweeter garlic flavor than raw cloves, with a texture like asparagus or green beans. They are versatile and can be eaten raw (in pesto), sautéed, grilled, roasted, or blended into soups and sauces, often used as a substitute for garlic or scallions. To prepare, trim the woody ends and the flower bud, then cook them until tender, or use them raw in pesto.",
